// Into Exile — ayodhya kanda
// Source: Valmiki, Ayodhya Kanda, sargas 20-46 (verify)
// Migrated from the old script format. Not yet staged for the Ramlila stage.

>> scene chamber
>> music dark
>> cast kaushalya at 0.66 face=left
>> cast rama:prince at 0.38
>> cast lakshmana:prince at 0.2
Rama goes first to his mother. Kaushalya is at her morning prayers, dressed for her son's crowning.
RAMA: Mother. I am not to be crowned. I am to go to the forest for fourteen years. I have come for your blessing.
She does not cry out. She stands exactly as she was, holding the lamp, and the flame does not move.
>> pose lakshmana point
LAKSHMANA: This is the work of one woman and one weak old man. Give me the word, brother. I will put you on that throne by noon.
RAMA: Put the bow down, Lakshmana. If I take the kingdom by breaking my father's word, what have I taken?
>> pose lakshmana stand
>> enter sita:bride from right to 0.84 in 1.4
RAMA: Sita. Stay with my mother. The forest is thorns and hunger and sleeping on the ground.
SITA: A forest where you are is a palace. A palace where you are not is a forest.
LAKSHMANA: And I walk in front with the bow. I am not asking.
>> enter sumitra from left to 0.06 in 1.2
SUMITRA: Go, my son. Think of Rama as your father, and of Sita as me, and of the forest as Ayodhya.
>> scene city clear
>> enter rama:prince from left to 0.3 in 0.1
>> enter sita:bride from left to 0.44 in 0.1
>> enter lakshmana:prince from left to 0.58 in 0.1
>> enter citizen from right to 0.8 in 0.6
>> enter citizen2 from right to 0.9 in 0.8 as=sage
>> pose citizen give
>> pose citizen2 give
Before they go, they give away everything they own.
>> play dragPlace \{"hint":"exile.11","keep":false,"items":\[\{"kind":"ornament","who":"rama","fy":190,"to":\[0.8,120\],"text":"exile.12"\},\{"kind":"ornament","who":"rama","fy":110,"to":\[0.9,120\]\},\{"kind":"ornament","who":"sita","fy":150,"to":\[0.8,120\],"text":"exile.13"\},\{"kind":"ornament","who":"sita","fy":90,"to":\[0.9,120\]\},\{"kind":"ornament","who":"lakshmana","fy":180,"to":\[0.8,120\],"text":"exile.14"\},\{"kind":"ornament","who":"lakshmana","fy":110,"to":\[0.9,120\]\}\]\}
>> set rama stage=exile
>> set lakshmana stage=exile
>> set sita stage=exile
Kaikeyi's women bring bark cloth. The brothers put it on. Sita holds hers and does not know how it is tied.
>> scene tamasa clear
>> music grief
Sumantra drives them out. The whole city follows on foot, and at nightfall lies down around the chariot on the bank of the Tamasa.
RAMA: They will follow us into the forest and starve there. We must be gone before they wake.
>> play drive \{\}
At dawn the people of Ayodhya wake to wheel tracks that lead toward the city and then are lost. They go home.
>> scene road clear
By then the chariot is at the edge of the kingdom.
-> END
